<H1>Medium data</H1>
Search for medium no. = [1227].
<HR>
Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121&#176;C for 15 min.
<HR>
<P><B><FONT SIZE=3>1227&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ZESTOSPHAERA MEDIUM</FONT></B></P>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Modified Brock's salt base solution (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=165">165</a>)   </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> L  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Na<sub>2</sub>S<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>&#183;5H<sub>2</sub>O                          </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;2.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> NaOH                                                    </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.16&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Resazurin                                               </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Trace mineral solution (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=446">446</a>)          </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;10.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water                                         </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> L  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Heat the medium to boiling while bubbling with a N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (4:1, v/v) gas mixture.  After boiling, cool the medium in a water bath.  Continue bubbling with the same gas mixture.  While the medium is still warm, add the following:  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Yeast extract (Oxoid)                                   </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Tryptone                                                </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Casamino acids (BD-Difco)                                          </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> L-Cystein&#183;HCl&#183;H<sub>2</sub>O                        </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.0625&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
After the medium is cooled to room temperature, adjust pH to 6.0 - 6.1.  Dispense the medium into culture vessels (e.g., 10 ml in Balch type tubes) under the same gas mixture, seal with butyl rubber stoppers and autoclave.       <br>
